[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2685620004","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103325#issuecomment-2685620004","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103325","id":2685620004,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gE08k","user":{"login":"hsandt","id":1067772,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNjc3NzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1067772?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsandt","html_url":"https://github.com/hsandt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsandt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsandt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsandt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsandt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsandt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsandt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsandt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsandt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsandt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-26T16:46:46Z","updated_at":"2025-02-26T16:46:46Z","body":"I found out a case where it matters to think whether we're having an `@export`ed or runtime `@onready` var: when designating other nodes.\n\n`@onready var node: Node2D = $\"Path/To/Node` is convenient but won't be usable in tool script.\n\nWhereas `@export var node: Node2D` + manual assignment will allow tool script to access that node.\n\nAlthough both are similar and work the same at runtime.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2685620004/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2686341605","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103325#issuecomment-2686341605","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103325","id":2686341605,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gHlHl","user":{"login":"jinyangcruise","id":42859362,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyODU5MzYy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42859362?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise","html_url":"https://github.com/jinyangcruise","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-26T22:22:44Z","updated_at":"2025-02-26T22:22:44Z","body":"Adding `@tool` to your NodeA may solve the problem.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2686341605/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2687853445","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103325#issuecomment-2687853445","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103325","id":2687853445,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gNWOF","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-27T12:42:37Z","updated_at":"2025-02-27T12:42:37Z","body":"Note that the documentation says:\n> Any other GDScript that your tool script uses must also be a tool. Any GDScript without `@tool` used by the editor will act like an empty file!","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2687853445/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3585239504","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103325#issuecomment-3585239504","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103325","id":3585239504,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7VsmnQ","user":{"login":"ColinSORourke","id":44822820,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0ODIyODIw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44822820?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke","html_url":"https://github.com/ColinSORourke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-27T10:56:39Z","updated_at":"2025-11-27T10:59:27Z","body":"I have tested this on Godot v4.6 Master and confirmed the behavior is entirely fixable in GDScript. The necessary information is all in the [@tool docs](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/plugins/running_code_in_the_editor.html).\n\nLike the previous commenters suggested, NodeB's `@tool` script cannot read a runtime variable NodeA's script because NodeA does not have the `@tool` annotation. \n\n> The general rule is that any other GDScript that your tool script uses must *also* be a tool. The editor is not able to construct instances from GDScript files without @tool, which means you cannot call methods or reference member variables from them otherwise.\n\nAdding the `@tool` annotation to Class_Name A makes all of the code work as intended, once the project has been relaunched. Relaunching is currently necessary because of the way Tool scripts are instantiated and updated, which is mentioned in the docs.\n\n> You may need to restart the editor. This is a known bug found in all Godot 4 versions: [GH-66381](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/66381).\n\nAs for your 2nd comment, `@onready var node: Node2D = $\"../NodeA\"` is accessible by a tool script, and is another element that currently cannot be hot-reloaded. Writing that line into a tool script and immediately trying to use that var will produce an error, but once the project has been restarted, the variable is initialized correctly and can be accessed regularly by the tool script without error.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3585239504/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]